Hello. I wanted to create a perl script that removes all the duplicate lines from a file. So I searched on google for some scripts that do that. But they don't work properly. I need a script that removes all duplicates, but also the blank lines, spaces and tabs.

Here's the script I've got now:
<code>use strict;
use warnings;
my $passwdfile = "d.txt";
my %seen = ();
{
   local @ARGV = ($passwdfile);
   local $^I = '.bac'; 
   while(<>){
   	  $_ =~ s/^\s+//;
      $seen{$_}++;
      next if $seen{$_} > 1;
      print;
   }
}
print "finished";</code>

